module gunbc.plans.shell_emission_model

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetirement, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { p }
import gunbc.design_ruling { project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts }



fn shell_emission_model_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    p(text: "**Goal:** medium-independent orchestration intent → emit(intent,Bash), with one intent authority and minimal shell. Extend the existing orchestration dispatcher; never restore ShellProgram/serialize_bash/program.dag (deleted #6831). v2.std.orchestration owns Run/Step/Pipeline/Predicate; v2.extdeps.languages.bash owns grammar; std.layout.Doc owns layout only. Do not mint EnsurePackage/EnableService/ServePort verbs for live_deploy: desugar their checks inline and consume host_effect.Policy.OneShotIdempotent."),
    p(text: "**Scope rule:** emit shell only for foreign executors requiring it (GHA run, cron, autoinstall, hooks) or bootstrap before a runtime/typed transport exists. Runtime-present work uses typed argv/service operations, typed transports or binary-interpreted effect plans with typed receipts; an opaque imperative driver is not a replacement. New non-thin shell needs a live leak fact, roster, dissolve trigger and sign-off. Every grammar/intent/desugar construct needs a named live emitting site; do not grow ingest gates for emit-only coverage. Bash remains an ordinary medium with explicit DecodeFidelity and typed refusal for ambiguous input. The provisioning-window executor capability design owns authorize_shell_emission and M0–M3."),
    p(text: "**Effects:** HostEffect.ShellCommand, ShellOnHost and the empty-script placeholder are deleted; retained_srvn bodies are a separate remaining population. host_effect_plan_apply records absent intent when no effect is attempted and actual intent for Do. Run.command:String remains an anemic seam whose target is Do\{effect\} with typed leaves. Load-bearing host_effect work remains behind srv3 OsInstalled and receipt-lock #5725 prerequisites; carrier deletion alone does not prove retained scripts dissolved."),
    p(text: "**Validation:** emit-only faithfulness needs executed equality against independently frozen committed bytes plus a one-byte perturbation RED. Typecheck, emission or comparing a producer with itself is insufficient. live_deploy’s historical self-comparison was the #6023 trap; its witness_script_producers_note owns replacement coverage. As runtime-present work it should become typed Filesystem.Write plus apt/systemctl/tailscale argv, not acquire a new permanent shell golden. Existing foreign-media file bodies are transport data; distinguish them from raw control flow by model walk."),
    p(text: "**Status authority:** gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_authority, not this prose. [Dated slice receipts and carve history](https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/blob/06d3c1c3149a7420c4a548b9aba9b15c721c635d/dag/gunbc/plans/shell_emission_model.dag) record Slice 0 #6467, Slice 1 #6475/#6566, and Slice 2 #6572/#6585/#6598 merged with operator sign-off still pending at that reading. Do not redispatch implemented work from stale census sizes; only the operator supplies signed(...) completion. fleet-converge.sh was subsequently deleted by #7121, so it is not a current golden."),
    p(text: "**Retained emission contract:** Retry threads on_exhausted; rejected CI retry emission uses ci_retry_emit_refused_poison to fail both workflow drift and YAML parsing, never a hand-spelled fallback. Environment framing uses EnvUnset/EnvPrefixed. If supports else and ExitZero/StrEq/StrEmpty/StrNonempty/LogMatches/Not/And/Or; scope also includes sequencing, pipes, command substitution, exit propagation, AndOr, redirects including append, env/set framing and TargetArchitecture dispatch. For refuses by design: runtime loops use typed folds/Retry, not new bash. Trap/background/functions/arrays/arithmetic/process substitution lacked sanctioned pre-runtime sites in the census. #7303 refuses multi-step Retry bodies, redirect/capture, changed log sources and N-level escalation; #7318 refuses nonempty source Run.env while preserving empty-env bytes."),
    p(text: "**While frontier:** #6832 added emission; #6718 removed the inert bound field. BoundedPoll never gained a production constructor and was deleted after a discriminating Node construction census (field-carrying construction edges prove an empty population; fieldless declarations receive no verdict). #14467 removed ci_floor_peak_emit and its only production While constructor; #14688 removed undiscovered orchestration_while_emit self-tests (orchestration_while_emit_test never named a module). PipelineStep::While and orch_emit_while_step remain for gunbc.plans.for_while_loop_sugar, but no executed witness established While byte rendering at the audit head. gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.witness_module_absent_from_the_executed_set option (c) owns the missing coherence witness. #14489’s path_predicate_bash_lowering_witness proves path predicate/dirname ascent bytes, not While."),
    p(text: "**Closed by deletion:** #7978’s cgroup vertical had typed path/procfs sources; its later-deleted bash_proc_self_cgroup bridge, NearestAncestorContaining/ascent helpers, calibration leaves and membership scan are historical, not open Phase-2 typing tasks. extdeps.linux.proc_self_cgroup.read_unified_cgroup_membership is the surviving typed reader; bash_path_predicate_target_model/bash_dirname_ascent_target_model retain their executed lowering witnesses. Phase 1 remains partial because While lacks a live constructor/witness and Run.command remains String; adoption versus explicit narrowing is still open."),
    p(text: "**Remaining work:** Slice 3 live_deploy typed effects; Slice 4 bmc token federation, CI inline RunSteps and thin pre-push ensure-built/exec claim_batch --pre-push with stdin passed through (move parsing/rosters/loops into the typed binary). live_deploy_remote_mutation_service_op_realization_dissolution_trigger binds tree_sync_restart_step_with_diagnosis and retires with it. The sidecar is already gone; intent Categories A–C remain owned by docs/plans/shell-intent-emit-realization-design.md and the residual census. **Open decisions:** Q3 move bespoke emit_orchestration dispatch into translate.target_model_edge_translation_rules or explicitly accept bridges; Q4 resolve duplicate extdeps.shell identities through dependency-pool precedence or the cross-tree consolidation. Current authority must settle those before implementation."),
  ]
}

data shell_emission_model_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly { ruling: project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts },
  slug: "shell-emission-model",
  title: "Shell emission model — orchestration intent to bash via emit(intent, Bash)",
  body: shell_emission_model_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Delete this doc when all shell-emit sites route through emit(intent,Bash), host_effect Phase B has dissolved ShellCommand\{script\} onto modeled orchestration intent, and no Category A–C intent-layer site remains in source (a residual census is not a prerequisite: retired by the 2026-10-30 process ruling, `gunbc.design_ruling bad_process_is_worse_than_no_process`; this does not establish corpus-wide coverage). (`program.dag` sidecar deletion is complete — #6831.)")
  }
}
